# Line endings, pinned where they matter.
#
# This project is edited on Windows and runs on Linux (a GitHub runner, and
# Cloudflare's build container), so the two ends have to agree.
#
# Two files must be LF *in the repository* whatever the working tree uses,
# because they are consumed on Linux and a CRLF one fails there rather than
# merely looking untidy: a CRLF `run:` block is a shell error on the runner, and
# `_headers` is parsed by Cloudflare. Naming them here makes that a property of
# the repository instead of a property of whichever machine did the commit.
#
# The rest of the text files are deliberately left unpinned: they are stored as
# LF and checked out as each platform prefers (this checkout has
# `core.autocrlf=true`, so the working copies are CRLF). Nothing else here reads
# raw bytes — the pages are HTML, and the renderer normalises newlines itself.

_headers                  text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yml   text eol=lf

# The build and its tests run on both.
tools/*.mjs               text eol=lf
tools/lib/*.mjs           text eol=lf
